; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Bubble Sort Bars
; CATEGORY: Algorithms
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     sorting, arrays, animation, loops
; SUMMARY:  Watch bubble sort push the tallest bars to the right, one swap at a time.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Twenty bars of random height appear in a row. Bubble sort walks
;   along the row comparing neighbors. The two bars being compared turn
;   yellow, and if the left one is taller they swap places. After each
;   pass the tallest unsorted bar has "bubbled" to the end and turns green.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Change the number in "make "size 20" near the
;   top of the code for more or fewer bars, or change :delay to slow it down.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * storing numbers in an ARRAY and changing them with SETITEM
;   * nested FOR loops
;   * swapping two values with a temporary variable
;   * drawing filled rectangles with FILLED
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Count the swaps and print the total at the end.
;   * Stop early when a whole pass makes no swaps. How much faster is it
;     on a list that is already nearly sorted?
;   * Make the bars sort from tallest to shortest instead.
; ============================================================

make "size 20
make "delay 4

; Fill an array with random heights between 10 and 250.
to make.bars :n
  make "bars array :n
  for [i 1 :n] [setitem :i :bars 10 + random 241]
end

; One bar is a filled rectangle standing on the line y = -200.
; The width of every bar depends on how many there are, so the row
; always fits across the screen.
to draw.bar :i :colr
  localmake "w 640 / :size
  penup
  setxy -320 + (:i - 1) * :w -200
  setheading 0
  pendown
  filled :colr [repeat 2 [forward item :i :bars  right 90  forward :w - 2  right 90]]
end

; Redraw everything. Bars from :done onwards are already in their final
; place, so they get a different color. :a and :b are being compared.
to show.bars :a :b :done
  clean
  for [i 1 :size] [
    ifelse or :i = :a :i = :b [draw.bar :i "yellow] [
      ifelse :i >= :done [draw.bar :i "#32cd32] [draw.bar :i "#4682b4]]
  ]
  wait :delay
end

to swap :a :b
  localmake "temp item :a :bars
  setitem :a :bars item :b :bars
  setitem :b :bars :temp
end

; Each pass compares neighbors from the left up to the last unsorted bar.
; After pass number p, the last p bars are in place, which is why the
; inner loop gets one step shorter every time.
to bubble.sort
  for [pass 1 :size - 1] [
    for [j 1 :size - :pass] [
      show.bars :j :j + 1 :size - :pass + 2
      if (item :j :bars) > (item :j + 1 :bars) [swap :j :j + 1]
    ]
  ]
  show.bars 0 0 1
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground "black
make.bars :size
bubble.sort
print [Bubble sort finished.]
